<Callout>
  <p><b>Check before you start.</b> If you have not exercised for some time, or you have a medical condition or any concern, speak to a GP first. The official <a href="https://eparmedx.com/" rel="noopener">PAR-Q+ questionnaire</a> is a free way to check whether you should.</p>
  <p><b>Not covered here:</b> under-18s, pregnancy and the first months after birth, older adults with frailty, anyone with a heart, lung, joint or nerve condition, and anyone with a current injury. Ask a doctor, physiotherapist or qualified exercise professional for a plan that fits you.</p>
  <p><b>During any session:</b> a dull muscle effort is expected. Stop for chest pain, dizziness, breathlessness that does not settle, or sharp, pinching or joint pain. Pain at 2 out of 10 or lower that is gone by the next morning is acceptable. Anything more is a signal to use the easier version.</p>
</Callout>
